{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1541430-apothecary-kith","id":1541430,"title":"Apothecary Kith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-02T20:10:56-07:00","id":1541430,"title":"Apothecary Kith","content":"I wrote this in sort-of response to the Chirurgeon kith in the Book of Seemings becoming more surgical focused. I thought the game could still do with a straight healer type like the original Chirurgeon in first edition. I realise that changelings have access to various healing abilities, so you may find this version 'underpowered' or flat out redundant. Still, here it is. Please feel free to critique.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:48px\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Vivaldi\"><span style=\"color:#76923c\">Apothecary</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"color:#76923c\"><i>Take this every morning before food.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\">Chirurgeons perform surgeries, but the Gentry also have need for medical generalists as well. They steal anyone who has ever shown an interest in keeping other things alive, including children who make \u2018medicines\u2019 for their dolls. In Arcadia, they learn everything about herbs and chemicals for curative use, usually through agonising self-medication. They often escape through the inventive use of some sleeping draught on their jailors.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Beast:</i> With both serpent and avian aspects, she can give an obstinate patient <i>such</i> a look. No one messes with her twice.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Darkling:</i> Always hidden behind a black mask and lab coat, he always seems to have whatever medicine is needed secreted upon his person.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Elemental:</i> She smells of a mix of lavender, aloe and tea tree. Flowers and herbs tangle among her hair and her skin has a sheen of fragrant oils.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Fairest:</i> His kind smile, soothing voice and beatific presence go a long way in the healing process.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Grimm:</i> Definitely a doctor. He wears doctor clothes and a stethoscope. He has a medical certificate on his person. Definitely a doctor.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Ogre:</i> She's a massage therapist who uses some interesting lotions and kneading techniques. Are you being cured, or <i>cured</i>?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Wizened:</i> He talks at a thousand words a minute, blinding customers with science. But don't call him a quack; his remedies work, dammit.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><b>Kith Blessing:</b> An Apothecary gains an exceptional success with three successes whenever they use Science or Medicine to diagnose or treat known diseases and poisons.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Potions, Pills and Tonics:</i> Once a day, so long as they have a goblin fruit to hand, the Apothecary may spend a point of Glamour to allow all injured people in his immediate vicinity to roll Stamina + Wyrd to downgrade success levels of damage. The goblin fruit is used up. They may do so more often, but each activation thereafter costs a point of Willpower as well.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8297,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8297-greg-davis","user":"Greg Davis","date":". 09-03-2024, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8297-greg-davis","name":"Greg Davis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T11:08:51-07:00","id":1541467,"title":"","content":"Maybe Potions Pills and Tonics could be reflavored, seems to be a pretty potent Ability","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T12:52:31-07:00","id":1541479,"title":"","content":"I did originally have it once a day. Perhaps I'll rejig it either to that or include a point of Willpower as well as the Glamour.<br /> <br /> Edit: I chose to do both. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> One free go, and then a Willpower point to the cost after that. This allows desperate changelings to burn through a valuable resource in order to stave off a bad situation, kind of like the party's 'cleric', but is expensive enough that they'll think twice about it in the normal course of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8297,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8297-greg-davis","user":"Greg Davis","date":". 09-03-2024, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8297-greg-davis","name":"Greg Davis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}